inil on counter-regulatory and cognitive responses to hypoglycaemia. <source>Diabetologia</source> <volume>47</volume>: <fpage>1704</fpage>&#x02013;1711, <year>2004</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15517154</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r49"><label>49</label><citation citation-type="journal">Bingham E, Hopkins D, Pernet A, Reid H, Macdonald IA, Amiel SA: The effects of KATP channel modulators on counterregulatory responses and cognitive function during acute controlled hypoglycaemia in healthy men: a pilot study. <source>Diabet Med</source> <volume>20</volume>: <fpage>231</fpage>&#x02013;237, <year>2003</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12675669</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r50"><label>50</label><citation citation-type="journal">Raju B, Cryer PE: Loss of the decrement in intraislet insulin plausibly explains loss of the glucagon response to hypoglycemia in insulin-deficient diabetes: documentation of the intraislet insulin hypothesis in humans. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>54</volume>: <fpage>757</fpage>&#x02013;764, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15734853</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r51"><label>51</label><citation citation-type="journal">Briscoe VJ, Ertl AC, Tate DB, Dawling S, Davis SN: Effects of a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor, fluoxetine, on counterregulatory responses to hypoglycemia in healthy individuals. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>57</volume>: <fpage>2453</fpage>&#x02013;2460, <year>2008</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18567822</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r52"><label>52</label><citation citation-type="journal">Porcellati F, Pampanelli S, Rossetti P, Busciantella Ricci N, Marzotti S, Lucidi P, Santeusanio F, Bolli GB, Fanelli CG: Effect of the amino acid alanine on glucagon secretion in non-diabetic and type 1 diabetic subjects during hyperinsulinaemic euglycaemia, hypoglycaemia and post-hypoglycaemic hyperglycaemia. <source>Diabetologia</source> <volume>50</volume>: <fpage>422</fpage>&#x02013;430, <year